These vectors are the `testdata/input` and `testdata/outhex` directories of
https://github.com/cyberphone/json-canonicalization at commit
19d51d7fe467d4706a3ff08adf8a748f29fc21e0 (2024-12-13), the reference test suite for
RFC 8785 (JSON Canonicalization Scheme), copyright 2018 Anders Rundgren, Apache License 2.0
(see LICENSE beside this file). Copied unchanged.

`input/<name>.json` is a JSON document; `outhex/<name>.txt` is the expected canonical
serialisation as space-separated hexadecimal UTF-8 bytes. The runner feeds each input to the
adapter's `canonicalise` and compares the bytes.

Not vendored: `testdata/output` (the same expectation as text, which editors and transfers can
mangle) and the 100-million-number file `es6testfile100m.txt.gz`, which is generated
deterministically by `testdata/numgen.go` or `numgen.js` in the upstream repository and is the
right thing to run once when porting the number formatter to a language whose float printing is
not ECMAScript's.
